.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-gist 1  "snip 0.5.4" 
.SH NAME
snip\-gist \- Publish snippets to GitHub Gists through the gh CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip gist\fR [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publish snippets to GitHub Gists through the gh CLI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
snip\-gist\-push(1)
Create the snippet\*(Aqs gist, or update it when one already exists
.TP
snip\-gist\-url(1)
Print the URL of the snippet\*(Aqs gist
.TP
snip\-gist\-status(1)
Report whether a snippet\*(Aqs gist is current
.TP
snip\-gist\-attach(1)
Record an existing gist as this snippet\*(Aqs gist
.TP
snip\-gist\-detach(1)
Forget a snippet\*(Aqs gist without deleting it on GitHub
.TP
snip\-gist\-delete(1)
Delete the snippet\*(Aqs gist on GitHub and forget it
.TP
snip\-gist\-open(1)
Open the snippet\*(Aqs gist in a browser
